### 6.2 · What is new, and where it lives

| piece | what it is | why it is not `winSE` |
|---|---|---|
| `stats.ts` `wilson` | score interval, optionally inflated for clustering | stays in [0,1], inverts the test a ceiling comparison *is* |
| `stats.ts` `clopper` | exact interval, by bisection on the binomial tails | conservative; it is what the verdicts are read off |
| `stats.ts` `binomTailGE` | exact one-sided p-value against a fixed rate | a ceiling is one-sided; an SE bar is not |
| `stats.ts` `designEffect` | ICC and variance inflation over the seed clusters | 223 matches are not 223 observations until this says so |
| `stats.ts` `mcnemar` | exact paired test on discordant matches | the same-seeds design is thrown away without it |
| `stats.ts` `sampleFor`/`sampleForExact` | the n at which a rate separates from the ceiling | turns "run more matches" into a number |
| `stats.ts` `exactLoAbove` | "does the exact lower bound clear the ceiling", by one tail sum | the long form spends 200 bisections on it, and wedged the first deep render |
| `targets.ts` `verdictOf` | INSIDE / OVER / **UNRESOLVED** | a two-state verdict cannot say "the run does not know" |
| `harness/mirrors` `mergeSections` | folds sharded seed spans into one section | the deep run is unaffordable single-file |
| `harness/cli` `--from` | seeds `[s, s+n)` | what makes a shard addressable |

Everything above is pinned in `tests/harness/a0-126-interval.test.ts`, each
against a value computed some other way: Wilson against its closed form,
Clopper–Pearson against the definition it is a bisection for, the binomial tails
against a hand enumeration of four coin flips, `zFor` against the textbook
quantiles so nothing hardcodes 1.96, and the design effect against two
constructed extremes. One of those tests is this report's headline, so that a
finding which stops being true fails a test before it misleads a reader.

